# This repository is written on Windows and runs on Linux.
#
# Git converts line endings in the working copy, which is fine for source
# files and fatal for shell scripts: a provision.sh checked out with CRLF
# fails on the server with
#
#   /usr/bin/env: 'bash\r': No such file or directory
#
# which says nothing about line endings and costs an hour to work out. These
# files are LF wherever they land.
*.sh      text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
*.yml     text eol=lf
*.yaml    text eol=lf
Caddyfile text eol=lf
.env.example text eol=lf

# Everything else: normalised in the repository, native in the working copy.
* text=auto
